  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "887c22c7-2074-4ed2-ae2d-53ea9f948737",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -6288,
        4560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "#FFC800",
        "width": 960,
        "height": 848,
        "content": "## AI Kubernetes Troubleshooting Agent\n\n### How it works\n1. A pod/node failure alert (or a manual test run) triggers the workflow.\n2. It collects kubectl events, logs, resource usage, and deployment state for the affected resource.\n3. Claude diagnoses the likely root cause and proposes one remediation action with a risk level.\n4. Safe actions auto-execute; riskier ones wait for human approval in Slack.\n5. After the fix, the workflow re-checks cluster health and closes the incident — or escalates to on-call if the symptoms persist.\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Add credentials for your cluster diagnostics/action API (never give this workflow raw kubeconfig/cluster-admin credentials directly)\n- [ ] Add Anthropic Claude, Slack, and incident/ticketing credentials\n- [ ] Edit Set - Config with your API URLs, auto-executable action list, Slack channels, and health-check thresholds\n- [ ] Point Wait - For Remediation Approval's resume webhook at your on-call tool's approve/reject action\n- [ ] Run once from Manual Trigger - Test Run against a known-bad namespace to confirm the full flow works"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7f569586-4dba-4498-9a1a-d08c10d63e29",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Stage 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -5088,
        4528
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 740,
        "height": 804,
        "content": "## Collect cluster diagnostics\n\nTakes the failure alert (or a manual test run), sets config, and pulls kubectl events, logs, resource usage, and deployment state for the affected resource."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "860a24c2-547f-47ad-b70b-4b397a80e87f",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Stage 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -4224,
        4544
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 648,
        "height": 1036,
        "content": "## Diagnose and gate on risk\n\nClaude proposes a root cause and remediation with a risk level; safe actions skip ahead, riskier ones wait on a Slack approval."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a831e34f-a9a9-4bbc-a77f-e33d67430451",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Stage 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3440,
        4528
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1540,
        "height": 1188,
        "content": "## Execute, verify, and close\n\nApplies the approved fix, waits for the cluster to stabilize, then verifies health and either closes the incident or escalates to on-call if it's still broken."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
